.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
.\" sigma-pkg(1) — SigmaOS package manager
.TH SIGMA-PKG 1 "2026-06-27" "SigmaOS" "SigmaOS User Commands"

.SH NAME
sigma-pkg \- install, remove, update, and manage SigmaOS packages

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sigma-pkg
.IR command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ package... ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sigma-pkg
is the SigmaOS package manager. Every package is verified with a
SHA-256 + BLAKE2b dual hash and a Dilithium3 (ML-DSA-65) post-quantum
signature before installation. Packages are installed atomically via
OSTree; a failed install never corrupts the running system.

.SH COMMANDS

.TP
.BI "install " package...
Download, verify, and install one or more packages.
.RS
.nf
$ sigma-pkg install vim htop curl
.fi
.RE

.TP
.BI "remove " package...
Remove installed packages. Configuration files are preserved by default.
.RS
.nf
$ sigma-pkg remove vim
$ sigma-pkg remove --purge vim    # also remove config files
.fi
.RE

.TP
.BI "update " [package...]
Update all installed packages (or specified ones) to their latest version.
.RS
.nf
$ sigma-pkg update                 # update everything
$ sigma-pkg update vim             # update only vim
.fi
.RE

.TP
.B search " keyword"
Search the package repository by name, description, or HSN category.
.RS
.nf
$ sigma-pkg search accounting      # find accounting apps
$ sigma-pkg search "GST"
.fi
.RE

.TP
.BI "show " package
Display detailed package information: version, description, size, dependencies,
install path (/sigma/store/<hash>-<name>-<ver>/), and Dilithium3 signature.

.TP
.B list
List all installed packages with version and derivation hash.

.TP
.BI "rollback " [generation]
Roll back to a previous package generation (GNU Guix-style).
.RS
.nf
$ sigma-pkg rollback               # list available generations
$ sigma-pkg rollback 3             # roll back to generation 3
.fi
.RE

.TP
.BI "verify " package
Re-verify the integrity of an installed package (dual hash + signature).

.TP
.BI "import " file
Import a .spkg archive from disk (offline install).

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be installed/removed without making changes.

.TP
.B \-\-no\-verify
Skip signature verification (DANGEROUS — only for development).

.TP
.BI "\-\-profile " name
Use a non-default package profile (e.g. \fIca\fR, \fIdeveloper\fR, \fIhealth\fR).

.TP
.B \-\-offline
Do not contact the package repository (use local cache only).

.SH SECURITY
All packages are:
.IP \(bu 3
Verified with SHA-256 + BLAKE2b (dual hash)
.IP \(bu 3
Signed with Dilithium3 (ML-DSA-65, NIST FIPS 204)
.IP \(bu 3
Installed to /sigma/store/<derivation-hash>-<name>-<ver>/ (Guix-style)
.IP \(bu 3
Checked against the dm-verity root hash before activation

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Install Tally-compatible accounting app
$ sigma-pkg install sigma-accounts sigma-gst sigma-payroll

# Search for CA tools
$ sigma-pkg search --profile ca

# Verify all installed packages
$ sigma-pkg list | awk '{print $1}' | xargs sigma-pkg verify

# Offline install from USB
$ sigma-pkg import /media/usb/sigma-vim-9.1.0.spkg
.fi

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sigma/var/db/pkg/installed.json
Database of installed packages and their derivation hashes.

.TP
.I /sigma/var/generations/
Generation snapshots for rollback (one directory per generation).

.TP
.I /sigma/store/
Content-addressed package store (immutable).

.TP
.I /sigma/etc/pkg/sources.list
Package repository URLs.

